      "explanation": "<p>Molecules are aromatic if they are</p>\n<p>(1) Cyclic</p>\n<p>(2) Planar</p>\n<p>(3) Conjugated</p>\n<p>(4) Molecules who have (4n + 2) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> electrons [This is called Huckel's Rule]</p>\n<p>Aromatic compounds are highly stable.</p>\n<p>(a) <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wne3sx/d0a68a1a-2638-4b3b-a63d-db27add46497/d31cea20-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wne3sy.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3wne3sx/d0a68a1a-2638-4b3b-a63d-db27add46497/d31cea20-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wne3sy.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 24th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 203 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3wne3sx/d0a68a1a-2638-4b3b-a63d-db27add46497/d31cea20-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wne3sy.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3wne3sx/d0a68a1a-2638-4b3b-a63d-db27add46497/d31cea20-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wne3sy.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wne3sx/d0a68a1a-2638-4b3b-a63d-db27add46497/d31cea20-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wne3sy.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3wne3sx/d0a68a1a-2638-4b3b-a63d-db27add46497/d31cea20-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wne3sy.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3wne3sx/d0a68a1a-2638-4b3b-a63d-db27add46497/d31cea20-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wne3sy.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3wne3sx/d0a68a1a-2638-4b3b-a63d-db27add46497/d31cea20-e23e-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wne3sy.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>(1) Molecule is cyclic.</p>\n<p>(2) All atoms which are completing the cyclic ring have sp<sup>2</sup> hybridisation. So it is shape is planar. If any one atom is sp<sup>3</sup> hybridised then molecule shape will be non planar.</p>\n<p>(3) It is conjugated means all <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds are showing resonance with each other.</p>\n<p>So all atoms which are forming cyclic ring are perticipating in resonance. That is called conjugated.</p>\n<p>(b) <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wng83r/cf074da2-d5de-4171-9cda-4dc15d41d74f/0e0d9170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wng83s.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3wng83r/cf074da2-d5de-4171-9cda-4dc15d41d74f/0e0d9170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wng83s.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 24th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 203 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3wng83r/cf074da2-d5de-4171-9cda-4dc15d41d74f/0e0d9170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wng83s.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3wng83r/cf074da2-d5de-4171-9cda-4dc15d41d74f/0e0d9170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wng83s.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wng83r/cf074da2-d5de-4171-9cda-4dc15d41d74f/0e0d9170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wng83s.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3wng83r/cf074da2-d5de-4171-9cda-4dc15d41d74f/0e0d9170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wng83s.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3wng83r/cf074da2-d5de-4171-9cda-4dc15d41d74f/0e0d9170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wng83s.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3wng83r/cf074da2-d5de-4171-9cda-4dc15d41d74f/0e0d9170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wng83s.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>(1) This compounds is cyclic</p>\n<p>(2) All atoms are sp<sup>2</sup> hybridised. So molecule shape is planar.</p>\n<p>(3) It is conjugated as all <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds are showing resonance.</p>\n<p>(4) It has 6<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>e<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup>. So obey Huckel Rule.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Compound is aromatic.</p>\n<p>(c) <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wnhp1d/0c8349fa-762d-4b5b-9a69-e4a6d79dbcc2/36f1b530-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnhp1f.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3wnhp1d/0c8349fa-762d-4b5b-9a69-e4a6d79dbcc2/36f1b530-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnhp1f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 24th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 203 English Explanation 3\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3wnhp1d/0c8349fa-762d-4b5b-9a69-e4a6d79dbcc2/36f1b530-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnhp1f.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3wnhp1d/0c8349fa-762d-4b5b-9a69-e4a6d79dbcc2/36f1b530-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnhp1f.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wnhp1d/0c8349fa-762d-4b5b-9a69-e4a6d79dbcc2/36f1b530-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnhp1f.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3wnhp1d/0c8349fa-762d-4b5b-9a69-e4a6d79dbcc2/36f1b530-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnhp1f.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3wnhp1d/0c8349fa-762d-4b5b-9a69-e4a6d79dbcc2/36f1b530-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnhp1f.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3wnhp1d/0c8349fa-762d-4b5b-9a69-e4a6d79dbcc2/36f1b530-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnhp1f.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>(1) This compound is cyclic</p>\n<p>(2) All atoms are sp<sup>2</sup> hybridised. So molecule shape is planar.</p>\n<p>(3) It is conjugated as <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond is showing resonance.</p>\n<p>(4) It has 2<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>e<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup>. So obey Huckel Rule.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Compound is aromatic.</p>\n<p>Anti-Aromatic :-</p>\n<p>It is highly unstable.</p>\n<p>Anti-aromatic compounds are -</p>\n<p>(1) Cyclic</p>\n<p>(2) All atoms which is forming cyclic ring are planar.</p>\n<p>(3) it is conjugated.</p>\n<p>(4) It has 4n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>e<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup>.</p>\n<p>Here no anti-aromatic compounds presents.</p>\n<p>Non-Aromatic :-</p>\n<p>Those compounds which are not either aromatic or anti-aromatic.</p>\n<p>Definition : All cyclic compounds which are comparatively stable with its open chain analogous system, compound is known as non aromatic compound.</p>\n<p>(a) <img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wnjzeu/5e81d995-3994-46db-8ecd-75065e6ffba6/76936170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnjzev.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3wnjzeu/5e81d995-3994-46db-8ecd-75065e6ffba6/76936170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnjzev.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 24th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 203 English Explanation 4\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3wnjzeu/5e81d995-3994-46db-8ecd-75065e6ffba6/76936170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnjzev.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3wnjzeu/5e81d995-3994-46db-8ecd-75065e6ffba6/76936170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnjzev.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wnjzeu/5e81d995-3994-46db-8ecd-75065e6ffba6/76936170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnjzev.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3wnjzeu/5e81d995-3994-46db-8ecd-75065e6ffba6/76936170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnjzev.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3wnjzeu/5e81d995-3994-46db-8ecd-75065e6ffba6/76936170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnjzev.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3wnjzeu/5e81d995-3994-46db-8ecd-75065e6ffba6/76936170-e23f-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnjzev.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Here one carbon is sp<sup>3</sup> hybridised that is why it's structure is non planar. So this cyclic compound will be neither aromatic nor anti-aromatic. It will be non aromatic.</p>\n<p>Multiple cyclic rings :-</p>\n<p>To find nature of this ring, make maximum possible <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds in the outer ring. This is a hypothetical structure. Here outer ring should be largest conjugated ring means outer ring should have these <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds which are in resonance with each other.</p>\n<p>And the nature of the outer ring will be same as the original molecule.</p>\n<p>(d)<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wnpwoc/dad26ed3-b88c-49c9-8b74-fe5ae4d59f3b/1b5125d0-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnpwod.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3wnpwoc/dad26ed3-b88c-49c9-8b74-fe5ae4d59f3b/1b5125d0-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnpwod.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 24th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 203 English Explanation 5\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3wnpwoc/dad26ed3-b88c-49c9-8b74-fe5ae4d59f3b/1b5125d0-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnpwod.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3wnpwoc/dad26ed3-b88c-49c9-8b74-fe5ae4d59f3b/1b5125d0-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnpwod.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wnpwoc/dad26ed3-b88c-49c9-8b74-fe5ae4d59f3b/1b5125d0-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnpwod.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3wnpwoc/dad26ed3-b88c-49c9-8b74-fe5ae4d59f3b/1b5125d0-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnpwod.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3wnpwoc/dad26ed3-b88c-49c9-8b74-fe5ae4d59f3b/1b5125d0-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnpwod.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3wnpwoc/dad26ed3-b88c-49c9-8b74-fe5ae4d59f3b/1b5125d0-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnpwod.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>From this structure we can't decide the nature as all <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds are not present in the outer ring that is why we make right resonating structure where all <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds present in the outer ring.</p>\n<p>Outer ring :</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wnsd4n/7970c7e2-296b-463d-9e9a-559fdcff9be7/5fa50f80-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnsd4o.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3wnsd4n/7970c7e2-296b-463d-9e9a-559fdcff9be7/5fa50f80-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnsd4o.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 24th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 203 English Explanation 6\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3wnsd4n/7970c7e2-296b-463d-9e9a-559fdcff9be7/5fa50f80-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnsd4o.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3wnsd4n/7970c7e2-296b-463d-9e9a-559fdcff9be7/5fa50f80-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnsd4o.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3wnsd4n/7970c7e2-296b-463d-9e9a-559fdcff9be7/5fa50f80-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnsd4o.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3wnsd4n/7970c7e2-296b-463d-9e9a-559fdcff9be7/5fa50f80-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnsd4o.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3wnsd4n/7970c7e2-296b-463d-9e9a-559fdcff9be7/5fa50f80-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnsd4o.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3wnsd4n/7970c7e2-296b-463d-9e9a-559fdcff9be7/5fa50f80-e240-11ec-9020-b7d4d48f3be3/file-1l3wnsd4o.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>As outer ring is aromatic so original compound will also be aromatic.</p>\n<p>Note :-</p>\n<p>Even though from left resonating structure we can't decide the nature of the molecule, it does not mean it's nature is not aromatic. As different resonating structures don't have different nature. All resonating structure have same nature.</p>"
